    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters September 2nd with a clear offensive engine powered by **Corbin Carroll** (81.56) and **James Wood** (76.28), our two highest-projected starters. **Corbin Carroll** benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Painter, where his elite speed profile remains a force multiplier despite the modest catcher pop time adjustment. Similarly, **James Wood** is set up for a productive afternoon against Holmes, supported by his superior xwOBA and a strong lead-off spot that maximizes his run-scoring opportunities. We also see high-floor production from **Josh Naylor** (65.83) and **Gabriel Moreno** (65.72), as both leverage soft-tossing opponents to provide critical stability across our 5x5 categories.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal threshold, ultimately leaving **Austin Riley** (49.59) on the bench. While **Austin Riley** offers legitimate power, his projection fell behind the likes of **Zach McKinstry** (41.81) and **Seiya Suzuki** (48.62) when adjusted for lineup positioning and specific platoon advantages. While **Seiya Suzuki** is facing a tough 2.19 xERA arm in Misiorowski\u2014a significant risk factor that suppressed his score\u2014he remains in the lineup due to his high base projection and favorable batting order. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Trevor Story** (55.19); although his score is solid, his position in the 8-hole and the SP\u2019s efficiency in holding runners limits his stolen base ceiling. We are strictly adhering to our 40-point \"Zebras Floor\" to preserve game caps, meaning **Travis Bazzana** (37.80) is firmly planted on the bench alongside the currently unranked **Mickey Moniak**, ensuring our remaining games are reserved for the highest-efficiency matchups.",
